> If I divide these by 72000 (correct?), I arrive at these values:

Why do you divide by 72000? The values are expressed in minutes so to get hours divide by 60. If the resulting values are not plausible then you used the incorrect column and decimal separator for your computer.

Please make sure parameters dec_report and sep_report in a way that matches you computer settings. GGIR's defaults assume that you are on a UK/US configured computer with dot separated decimals and comma separated columns.

> The other question is: Do you know which observation period is optimal to obtain a realistic impression of a patient? Many studies only give an outlook that it should be longer than 7 days and must also include a weekend, but there is no specification of 21 days, for example, right? We would like to start a study with a wearing time of just under one month with a recording frequency of 20Hz. Perhaps you can also give us your opinion on this.

Unfortunately, I cannot provide free advice on how to do your research. I only reply to questions in this group that relate to the clarity or correctness of GGIR. Maybe other members of the group want to chip in and share their thoughts.

